From ea8896ffbd77e4e7eb816eef81e343177ff04d63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:02:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libsensor: fix null-pointer crash in
 SensorManager::getSensorList

getSensorList() declared its output buffer as ASensorList* (i.e. a
pointer to ASensor const* const*) initialized to nullptr, then passed
that null pointer directly to ASensorManager_getSensorList() instead of
its address. The NDK function's real signature is
  int ASensorManager_getSensorList(ASensorManager*, ASensorList* list)
and writes the resulting array pointer through *list - so it
dereferenced the null pointer and crashed with SIGSEGV every time this
was called, before ever returning. The follow-up indexing
(`*aSensorList[i]`) was also one level of indirection off relative to
the (fixed) ASensorList typedef.

Fixed by declaring aSensorList as a plain ASensorList (matching the
typedef, ASensorRef const*) and passing &aSensorList, with indexing
corrected to match (aSensorList[i] directly yields an ASensorRef).

This is the actual crash site behind the gpsd/libsensor_vendor.so
SIGSEGV seen when something triggers sensor-assisted GNSS positioning
on gts210wifi - device/samsung/gts2-common's libshim_gpsd/libsensor.cpp
shim (separate repo) also had a related but distinct bug in the same
call chain (Singleton<SensorManager>::sLock/sInstance defined as empty
functions instead of real data), fixed alongside this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I4b61b4c8032a36e41870e7d83e2dd0410379b28d
---
 libsensor/SensorManager.cpp | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libsensor/SensorManager.cpp b/libsensor/SensorManager.cpp
index cfe46fc..c2eb01e 100644
--- a/libsensor/SensorManager.cpp
+++ b/libsensor/SensorManager.cpp
@@ -42,17 +42,17 @@ SensorManager::SensorManager() : mInitCheck(NO_INIT) {
 ssize_t SensorManager::getSensorList(Sensor const* const** list) {
     Mutex::Autolock autoLock(mLock);
 
-    ASensorList* aSensorList = nullptr;
+    ASensorList aSensorList;
     int count;
     ASensorRef aSensor;
 
-    count = ASensorManager_getSensorList(mASensorManager, aSensorList);
+    count = ASensorManager_getSensorList(mASensorManager, &aSensorList);
 
     mSensors = static_cast<Sensor const**>(malloc(count * sizeof(Sensor*)));
     assert(mSensors != nullptr);
 
     for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
-        aSensor = *aSensorList[i];
+        aSensor = aSensorList[i];
         mSensors[i] = new Sensor(aSensor);
     }
 
